{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 26, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1  \nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS OVERSIMPLIFIED TO THE POINT OF DANGEROUS AMBIGUITY. IT IMPLIES A CLEAR, OBJECTIVE STANDARD FOR WHAT CONSTITUTES A \"BAD\" LAW, YET OFFERS NO CRITERIA FOR DETERMINING THAT QUALITY. WITHOUT A FRAMEWORK FOR ASSESSING MORALITY, JUSTICE, OR LEGAL LEGITIMACY, THE STATEMENT INVITES SUBJECTIVE INTERPRETATION—WHICH CAN BE EXPLOITED TO JUSTIFY DISREGARD FOR LAWS BASED ON PERSONAL BIASES, POLITICAL AGENDAS, OR EVEN CIVIL DISOBEDIENCE WITHOUT ACCOUNTABILITY. IN A FUNCTIONING SOCIETY, LAWS ARE NOT MERELY MORAL STATEMENTS; THEY ARE INSTITUTIONALIZED NORMS THAT MAINTAIN ORDER, AND DISREGARD FOR THEM MUST BE GUIDED BY PROCEDURAL MECHANISMS, NOT INDIVIDUAL JUDGMENT.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2  \nFURTHERMORE, THE SENTENCE NEGLECTS THE COLLECTIVE AND HISTORICAL CONTEXT IN WHICH LAWS ARE MADE AND CHANGED. EVEN UNJUST LAWS OFTEN SERVE AS CATALYSTS FOR REFORM—AND DISREGARDING THEM WITHOUT LEGAL OR DEMOCRATIC CHANNELS CAN UNDERMINE THE VERY STRUCTURES THAT ENABLE CHANGE. HISTORY SHOWS THAT PROTEST, CIVIL DISOBEDIENCE, AND LEGAL CHALLENGES ARE THE APPROPRIATE PATHS TO CORRECT BAD LAWS, NOT UNILATERAL NONCOMPLIANCE. BY REDUCING COMPLEX ETHICAL AND LEGAL DYNAMICS TO A SIMPLE IF-THEN STATEMENT, THE SENTENCE ENCOURAGES A FORM OF INDIVIDUALISTIC ANARCHY THAT THREATENS THE RULE OF LAW. IT IS NOT ENOUGH TO DECLARE A LAW BAD—ONE MUST ACT TO CHANGE IT WITHIN THE SYSTEM, NOT BEYOND IT.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "AGR", "logprob": -1.6093124941107817e-05}, {"token": "APH", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -2.1576648578047752e-05}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "  \n", "logprob": -0.0059441933408379555}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.007676506415009499}, {"token": " SENT", "logprob": -0.016198454424738884}, {"token": "ENCE